1
00:01:01,520 --> 00:01:02,080
Here.

2
00:01:02,680 --> 00:01:03,320
Here.

3
00:01:06,080 --> 00:01:07,000
Hurry.

4
00:01:09,680 --> 00:01:10,560
Time is money.

5
00:01:10,680 --> 00:01:11,520
Just say it.

6
00:01:12,120 --> 00:01:13,200
We visited the market,

7
00:01:13,200 --> 00:01:14,000
found the shop,

8
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:15,400
and appraised the goods.

9
00:01:15,480 --> 00:01:16,840
We just need a translator to bargain.

10
00:01:16,840 --> 00:01:18,840
The boss only understands Hokkien.

11
00:01:21,039 --> 00:01:22,280
A translator is 28 yuan per hour,

12
00:01:22,280 --> 00:01:23,640
with a minimum of three hours.

13
00:01:23,640 --> 00:01:24,640
Good deal, right?

14
00:01:25,800 --> 00:01:27,680
Then I should thank you, Miss Li.

15
00:01:27,680 --> 00:01:28,760
You're welcome, Mr. Zhang.

16
00:01:28,760 --> 00:01:29,640
Hurry.

17
00:01:30,880 --> 00:01:31,800
I'm sorry

18
00:01:31,800 --> 00:01:33,720
for making you come all the way here.

19
00:01:33,720 --> 00:01:35,640
Is 'I'm sorry' your catchphrase?

20
00:01:35,960 --> 00:01:36,960
Watch your mouth.

21
00:01:37,880 --> 00:01:39,680
It's okay, she's just like that.

22
00:01:39,800 --> 00:01:40,720
I'm sorry.

23
00:01:40,800 --> 00:01:41,600
It's fine.

24
00:01:41,680 --> 00:01:43,120
Being able to say whatever you want

25
00:01:43,120 --> 00:01:44,000
is a good thing.

26
00:01:44,479 --> 00:01:46,080
It really is a catchphrase.

27
00:01:46,600 --> 00:01:47,280
Boss.

28
00:01:48,320 --> 00:01:49,250
How much is this?

29
00:01:49,280 --> 00:01:50,340
This is three yuan.

30
00:01:50,840 --> 00:01:51,640
Three.

31
00:01:54,600 --> 00:01:56,000
Let me carry that for you.

32
00:01:56,200 --> 00:01:57,400
Carrying it yourself

33
00:01:57,520 --> 00:01:58,850
is not very convenient.

34
00:01:59,080 --> 00:01:59,920
It's okay.

35
00:01:59,920 --> 00:02:00,880
It's not heavy.

36
00:02:00,880 --> 00:02:02,520
Besides, I'm used to it.

37
00:02:02,960 --> 00:02:04,600
Thank you so much today.

38
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:06,800
I couldn't find the place alone,

39
00:02:07,280 --> 00:02:08,880
and was afraid of buying the wrong things.

40
00:02:08,880 --> 00:02:11,240
Let alone travel agencies,

41
00:02:11,400 --> 00:02:13,080
even local guides wouldn't take such a small order.

42
00:02:13,080 --> 00:02:15,040
Thank you so much today.

43
00:02:15,080 --> 00:02:16,040
I'm sorry.

44
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:17,930
You're welcome.

45
00:02:18,320 --> 00:02:20,320
I got my tour guide certificate before,

46
00:02:20,320 --> 00:02:21,450
but never led a tour.

47
00:02:21,680 --> 00:02:24,079
This time, I finally experienced it.

48
00:02:26,520 --> 00:02:27,960
It's so beautiful.

49
00:02:31,040 --> 00:02:32,900
We should take more photos later.

50
00:02:33,040 --> 00:02:34,360
No problem.

51
00:02:34,480 --> 00:02:35,720
I'm so satisfied with my makeup today.

52
00:02:35,720 --> 00:02:36,920
It's rare for me to look this good.

53
00:02:36,920 --> 00:02:38,000
Did you notice?

54
00:02:38,360 --> 00:02:39,690
For their whole family,

55
00:02:39,840 --> 00:02:41,640
she's the one carrying all the bags.

56
00:02:41,640 --> 00:02:42,770
It's quite pitiful.

57
00:02:45,680 --> 00:02:47,340
What's the connection there?

58
00:02:48,600 --> 00:02:49,600
Besides, whether others are pitiful or not,

59
00:02:49,600 --> 00:02:51,000
what does it have to do with me?

60
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:52,400
Do you have any humanity?

61
00:02:52,840 --> 00:02:53,920
Such a big family,

62
00:02:53,920 --> 00:02:56,000
but they sent a young girl out to buy things alone.

63
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:58,280
It's so unsafe in an unfamiliar place.

64
00:02:58,880 --> 00:02:59,720
I'm sorry.

65
00:02:59,920 --> 00:03:01,380
My boyfriend loves these.

66
00:03:01,680 --> 00:03:04,440
It's rare for him to get time off and walk around with his family,

67
00:03:04,440 --> 00:03:05,840
so he asked me to buy them.

68
00:03:07,920 --> 00:03:08,780
What about you?

69
00:03:09,320 --> 00:03:09,960
Me?

70
00:03:10,160 --> 00:03:11,360
I'm fine with it.

71
00:03:11,880 --> 00:03:13,600
He brought me on his vacation,

72
00:03:14,880 --> 00:03:16,680
which is already troubling him.

73
00:03:21,079 --> 00:03:23,480
That crown from earlier looked quite nice.

74
00:03:24,440 --> 00:03:25,770
That's a Phoenix Crown.

75
00:03:26,160 --> 00:03:28,120
I even looked it up before coming here.

76
00:03:28,120 --> 00:03:30,850
It's the traditional dress of the She girls here.

77
00:03:31,360 --> 00:03:32,420
It's so beautiful.

78
00:03:33,120 --> 00:03:34,480
Since you're here,

79
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:36,260
why don't you try it on?

80
00:03:36,760 --> 00:03:37,420
No, thanks.

81
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:38,880
I'll just look.

82
00:03:40,800 --> 00:03:41,800
What if it's free?

83
00:03:48,280 --> 00:03:49,160
Excuse me.

84
00:03:49,160 --> 00:03:50,240
Is it really free?

85
00:03:50,360 --> 00:03:52,000
Fair and square.

86
00:03:54,360 --> 00:03:57,079
This guy is a friend I met while traveling.

87
00:03:57,280 --> 00:03:59,160
I promise it's not only free,

88
00:03:59,280 --> 00:04:01,140
but the results are also amazing.

89
00:04:01,440 --> 00:04:03,080
Hello, I'm makeup artist Tang Yi.

90
00:04:03,080 --> 00:04:04,880
You can choose a look here first.

91
00:04:04,880 --> 00:04:05,480
Go, go, go.

92
00:04:10,680 --> 00:04:12,200
So basically, all day,

93
00:04:12,400 --> 00:04:14,520
you've been running a losing business.

94
00:04:14,520 --> 00:04:17,560
Sister, for us in the service industry,

95
00:04:17,600 --> 00:04:20,730
the most important thing is the customer's experience.

96
00:04:21,760 --> 00:04:22,360
Alright.

97
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:24,000
Then you keep serving.

98
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:24,480
I'm leaving.

99
00:04:24,480 --> 00:04:25,080
Stop.

100
00:04:27,400 --> 00:04:29,360
Translation fees start at three hours.

101
00:04:29,360 --> 00:04:30,880
Your work is not done yet.

102
00:04:33,040 --> 00:04:34,040
Sorry.

103
00:04:34,200 --> 00:04:35,720
Does it look a bit weird?

104
00:04:35,720 --> 00:04:36,520
No.

105
00:04:37,240 --> 00:04:38,600
This is called the Phoenix Dress.

106
00:04:38,600 --> 00:04:41,080
It's the traditional clothing of She ethnic girls in Matou.

107
00:04:41,080 --> 00:04:42,340
It suits you very well.

108
00:04:43,560 --> 00:04:45,640
I don't mean the craftsmanship is bad.

109
00:04:45,640 --> 00:04:47,040
It's my own problem.

110
00:04:47,120 --> 00:04:49,560
I don't usually dress up.

111
00:04:50,880 --> 00:04:52,080
It's very beautiful.

112
00:04:52,240 --> 00:04:53,240
It suits you well.

113
00:04:54,120 --> 00:04:56,680
Isn't this a great service spirit?

114
00:04:59,720 --> 00:05:00,960
Since that's the case,

115
00:05:00,960 --> 00:05:03,440
let's provide a one-stop service to the end.

116
00:05:08,160 --> 00:05:09,120
Yes, exactly, come on.

117
00:05:09,120 --> 00:05:10,040
Strike a pose.

118
00:05:10,040 --> 00:05:11,080
Raise your hands.

119
00:05:11,080 --> 00:05:12,160
Not bad, not bad, not bad.

120
00:05:12,160 --> 00:05:13,520
Step forward.

121
00:05:13,520 --> 00:05:14,040
Right, right, right.

122
00:05:14,040 --> 00:05:15,760
Push forward.

123
00:05:16,120 --> 00:05:17,040
Right, right, right.

124
00:05:17,040 --> 00:05:18,920
A bit to the left.

125
00:05:18,920 --> 00:05:19,760
A bit more to the right.

126
00:05:19,760 --> 00:05:20,680
Blocking the face.

127
00:05:20,680 --> 00:05:21,480
Not blocking.

128
00:05:21,520 --> 00:05:22,250
Right, good.

129
00:05:22,640 --> 00:05:23,970
Go this way, go that way.

130
00:05:24,080 --> 00:05:25,040
Come, right.

131
00:05:25,440 --> 00:05:26,680
Bring it forward.

132
00:05:26,920 --> 00:05:28,240
Let's get a close-up.

133
00:05:28,560 --> 00:05:30,560
Sit down, right, good.

134
00:05:30,880 --> 00:05:32,520
Move back, come.

135
00:05:32,760 --> 00:05:34,080
Not bad, not bad, not bad.

136
00:05:34,080 --> 00:05:35,480
Looks good.

137
00:05:36,320 --> 00:05:37,800
Let's go take some shots over there.

138
00:05:37,800 --> 00:05:39,060
It looks better there.

139
00:05:39,720 --> 00:05:40,440
Let's go.

140
00:05:45,760 --> 00:05:46,920
Yes, look back.

141
00:05:47,440 --> 00:05:48,320
Where's the reflector?

142
00:05:48,320 --> 00:05:48,920
Here.

143
00:05:49,280 --> 00:05:50,080
Closer, yes.

144
00:05:50,080 --> 00:05:51,400
Up, right.

145
00:05:51,400 --> 00:05:52,840
Come look here.

146
00:05:53,200 --> 00:05:54,480
You're quite expressive on camera.

147
00:05:54,480 --> 00:05:56,010
Not your first time, right?

148
00:05:56,320 --> 00:05:57,480
I majored as a flight attendant,

149
00:05:57,480 --> 00:05:59,320
so I learned facial expression management.

150
00:05:59,320 --> 00:06:01,560
Later I met Zinan.

151
00:06:01,880 --> 00:06:03,760
He said it's not safe to fly everywhere,

152
00:06:03,760 --> 00:06:04,960
so he asked me to quit.

153
00:06:06,640 --> 00:06:07,840
Sorry, I digressed.

154
00:06:09,320 --> 00:06:11,240
So you were a flight attendant major.

155
00:06:11,240 --> 00:06:13,880
Does that mean you're not afraid of heights at all?

156
00:06:13,880 --> 00:06:16,200
I've loved being in high places since I was little.

157
00:06:16,200 --> 00:06:17,880
Looking down from the sky,

158
00:06:17,880 --> 00:06:20,880
everything on the ground seems insignificant.

159
00:06:21,320 --> 00:06:23,520
All the bad things and worries

160
00:06:23,520 --> 00:06:25,240
become so, so small.

161
00:06:25,920 --> 00:06:28,680
There's a paragliding base in Jiudu at Shanmei Reservoir.

162
00:06:28,680 --> 00:06:31,010
You can check it out if you're interested.

163
00:06:31,360 --> 00:06:32,080
I know.

164
00:06:32,400 --> 00:06:33,640
I really wanted to go before I came.

165
00:06:33,640 --> 00:06:35,040
I even made an itinerary.

166
00:06:35,480 --> 00:06:36,480
But later,

167
00:06:36,880 --> 00:06:37,840
his parents wanted to come too,

168
00:06:37,840 --> 00:06:40,400
and bringing his brother made it inconvenient.

169
00:06:40,400 --> 00:06:42,440
So you mean

170
00:06:42,920 --> 00:06:44,320
he made you quit your job,

171
00:06:44,640 --> 00:06:45,040
said he'd take you on a trip,

172
00:06:45,040 --> 00:06:46,280
said he'd take you on a trip,

173
00:06:46,280 --> 00:06:48,480
and ended up bringing his whole family.

174
00:06:49,159 --> 00:06:50,120
Focus on taking pictures.

175
00:06:50,120 --> 00:06:53,280
It's fine. Being in a relationship means accommodating each other.

176
00:06:53,280 --> 00:06:55,440
Although he doesn't like me going out to work,

177
00:06:55,440 --> 00:06:57,440
he treats me very well.

178
00:06:57,840 --> 00:06:59,920
He's my fiancé, after all.

179
00:07:03,400 --> 00:07:04,480
Your phone.

180
00:07:07,400 --> 00:07:08,040
Hello?

181
00:07:08,760 --> 00:07:10,560
Have you bought the seafood yet?

182
00:07:10,920 --> 00:07:12,280
You didn't overspend the money I gave you, did you?

183
00:07:12,280 --> 00:07:12,960
I bought it.

184
00:07:13,080 --> 00:07:14,560
There's still over 200 left.

185
00:07:14,560 --> 00:07:16,160
Zinan, I went to a travel...

186
00:07:16,160 --> 00:07:16,720
Alright.

187
00:07:17,440 --> 00:07:19,040
We'll talk when you get back.

188
00:07:20,080 --> 00:07:21,720
Mom, Dad, and my brother are hungry.

189
00:07:21,720 --> 00:07:22,920
We won't wait for you.

190
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:25,600
Just use the remaining money for your own meal.

191
00:07:27,280 --> 00:07:27,880
Wait.

192
00:07:28,560 --> 00:07:30,090
Do you want to eat together?

193
00:07:30,960 --> 00:07:32,440
Just spend a few dozen on your meal,

194
00:07:32,440 --> 00:07:33,900
and transfer the 200 to me.

195
00:07:34,120 --> 00:07:36,580
We'll pack some food for you after we finish.

196
00:07:43,560 --> 00:07:45,760
This brick is so red.

197
00:07:46,560 --> 00:07:47,400
Idiot.

198
00:07:47,600 --> 00:07:51,120
A traditional red brick house is naturally built with red bricks.

199
00:07:51,120 --> 00:07:52,880
Then I'll go back and take off my makeup.

200
00:07:52,880 --> 00:07:54,520
I'm really sorry about today.

201
00:07:54,520 --> 00:07:55,560
Sorry for the trouble.

202
00:07:55,560 --> 00:07:57,960
Then just come to the front desk to find us later,

203
00:07:57,960 --> 00:07:59,760
and we'll send the photos to you.

204
00:08:02,160 --> 00:08:02,760
It's fine.

205
00:08:07,280 --> 00:08:08,480
I'll get going then.

206
00:08:11,200 --> 00:08:12,040
No, no, no.

207
00:08:15,360 --> 00:08:16,880
Yiyi, this outfit...

208
00:08:19,640 --> 00:08:20,440
It looks nice,

209
00:08:20,480 --> 00:08:22,210
but it doesn't really suit you.

210
00:08:22,360 --> 00:08:23,160
Yiyi.

211
00:08:23,560 --> 00:08:24,240
Yiyi.

212
00:08:25,080 --> 00:08:26,480
This outfit looks great on you.

213
00:08:26,480 --> 00:08:27,480
It suits you so well.

214
00:08:27,480 --> 00:08:28,960
It's like it was tailor-made for you.

215
00:08:28,960 --> 00:08:29,520
Yeah.

216
00:08:29,800 --> 00:08:31,040
What are you wearing?

217
00:08:31,040 --> 00:08:32,000
It's too flashy.

218
00:08:32,440 --> 00:08:33,640
It's all a scam.

219
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:34,860
Let me tell you,

220
00:08:35,240 --> 00:08:37,320
Zinan works hard for his money.

221
00:08:37,320 --> 00:08:39,120
You can't just spend it casually.

222
00:08:39,120 --> 00:08:40,679
They did it for free.

223
00:08:40,679 --> 00:08:41,440
It didn't cost anything.

224
00:08:41,440 --> 00:08:42,960
It's free now,

225
00:08:42,960 --> 00:08:44,159
but what about when you're done?

226
00:08:44,159 --> 00:08:46,220
They'll definitely force you to buy.

227
00:08:46,240 --> 00:08:47,040
Don't you know?

228
00:08:47,040 --> 00:08:47,640
Yiyi.

229
00:08:47,880 --> 00:08:49,280
You look better without makeup.

230
00:08:49,280 --> 00:08:50,280
Come on, let's wash your face.

231
00:08:50,280 --> 00:08:51,920
We shouldn't take advantage of others.

232
00:08:51,920 --> 00:08:54,280
Now you know better than to take advantage.

233
00:08:54,280 --> 00:08:56,600
When you took advantage of the cab fare,

234
00:08:56,880 --> 00:08:57,920
you didn't say that.

235
00:08:57,920 --> 00:08:59,600
Yeah, why didn't you do this earlier?

236
00:08:59,600 --> 00:09:01,200
Thank you for your kindness,

237
00:09:01,360 --> 00:09:02,680
but Yiyi doesn't need this.

238
00:09:02,680 --> 00:09:03,400
She doesn't need it,

239
00:09:03,400 --> 00:09:04,000
but you do.

240
00:09:04,160 --> 00:09:04,680
All right.

241
00:09:04,680 --> 00:09:05,480
Let's go.

242
00:09:05,880 --> 00:09:07,140
It gives me a headache.

243
00:09:24,880 --> 00:09:25,600
Tell me,

244
00:09:25,720 --> 00:09:27,850
what did Lin Yiyi want to say at the end?

245
00:09:29,120 --> 00:09:30,180
It doesn't matter.

246
00:09:31,120 --> 00:09:32,250
You aren't curious?

247
00:09:32,320 --> 00:09:33,450
I don't believe you.

248
00:09:34,040 --> 00:09:34,760
You

249
00:09:35,040 --> 00:09:36,320
are just stubborn.

250
00:09:36,840 --> 00:09:38,520
I asked you to praise her and you wouldn't.

251
00:09:38,520 --> 00:09:40,120
But you did in the end anyway.

252
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:43,330
So what if I praised her?

253
00:09:43,560 --> 00:09:44,840
The result is the same.

254
00:09:45,800 --> 00:09:48,920
Nice guys finish last.

255
00:09:51,040 --> 00:09:51,840
Wait for me.

256
00:10:27,320 --> 00:10:28,720
Eight-treasure congee.

257
00:10:29,440 --> 00:10:30,480
How much is this?

258
00:10:31,400 --> 00:10:32,560
It's free.

259
00:10:34,040 --> 00:10:34,800
Thank you.

260
00:10:40,560 --> 00:10:43,160
My eight-treasure congee tastes good, right?

261
00:10:44,040 --> 00:10:44,880
But,

262
00:10:45,080 --> 00:10:47,080
what you said just now

263
00:10:47,080 --> 00:10:48,540
was actually pretty cool.

264
00:10:49,720 --> 00:10:51,960
Do you know how to pronounce these two words?

265
00:10:51,960 --> 00:10:52,800
Konjac.

266
00:10:53,880 --> 00:10:56,280
This didn't exist when I was in junior high.

267
00:10:57,360 --> 00:10:58,090
At that time,

268
00:10:58,560 --> 00:10:59,480
milk tea

269
00:10:59,800 --> 00:11:01,330
was still made from powder.

270
00:11:03,640 --> 00:11:05,280
I need a high-paying job

271
00:11:05,440 --> 00:11:06,760
with full benefits

272
00:11:06,840 --> 00:11:09,240
and steady salary increases every six months

273
00:11:09,240 --> 00:11:10,560
so I can buy

274
00:11:10,560 --> 00:11:12,420
my dream house within four years.

275
00:11:12,960 --> 00:11:13,760
God of Wealth,

276
00:11:14,040 --> 00:11:15,880
I pray to you so sincerely every day.

277
00:11:15,880 --> 00:11:17,010
You heard me, right?

278
00:11:17,280 --> 00:11:18,160
Did you?

279
00:11:28,480 --> 00:11:29,610
I'm editing photos.

280
00:11:30,120 --> 00:11:31,520
Which filter looks good?

281
00:11:38,200 --> 00:11:40,680
Not to mention travel agencies for such small orders,

282
00:11:40,680 --> 00:11:42,000
even local guides don't take them.
